; `docs/reference.md:917` says an operation colliding with a function
; is a duplicate definition. It was not implemented: this program
; checked clean, built, and trapped at run time with exit 71, no
; stdout and no stderr - the operation won the call and no handler was
; installed.
;
; An `effect` declares one value name per operation, the same way a
; `trait` declares one per method, so both now reach `checkDuplicates`
; through `declFields`.
(effect Two
  (two :: (-> Int Int Int)))

(:: two (-> Int Int))

(fn (two n) 5)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (two 3))
